## Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made:

**1. Package Installation:**
- Installed `@vercel/analytics@^2.0.1` using npm
- Updated `package.json` and `package-lock.json` with the new dependency

**2. Configuration:**
- Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to include the Analytics component
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Placed `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag as per official Vercel documentation

**3. Implementation Details:**
- Followed the official Vercel Analytics Quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart)
- Used framework-specific instructions for Next.js App Router
- Preserved existing code structure and formatting
- Maintained all existing imports and metadata configuration

**4. Verification:**
- ✓ TypeScript type checking passed
- ✓ ESLint linting passed with no errors
- ✓ Production build completed successfully
- ✓ All 13 tests passed (4 test files)
- ✓ Lock files updated correctly

### Files Modified:
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency tree
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics component

### Next Steps:
The Analytics component is now integrated. After deploying to Vercel:
1. Navigate to Analytics in your Vercel dashboard
2. Select your project and click "Enable"
3. Analytics will be available at `/_vercel/insights/*` routes
4. Verify functionality by checking Network tab for analytics requests

The implementation is complete and ready for deployment.
